SIDMon1.0 -- ONE WORD PATCHED, not the binary UADE ships.

  file offset 0x19C:  5288 -> 5488   (addq.l #1,a0 -> addq.l #2,a0)
  file offset 0x228:  5288 -> 5488   (ditto)

There are TWO byte-stepping scans, not one: InitPlayer hunts for the playroutine
entry, and patchjmps then walks the same region rewriting jmp -> rts. Patching
only the first just moves the address error to the second. Both were found by
searching the binary for the pattern `addq.l #1,a0` immediately followed by a
dbra, which is what a byte-stepping scan looks like; there are no other
occurrences of addq.l #1,a0 in this player.

WHY. UADE's SidMon eagleplayer locates the embedded playroutine by scanning the
module for an RTS followed by movem.l d0-d7/a0-a6,-(sp):

    initloop:   cmp.w  #$4e75,(a0)
                bne    nextinitloop
                cmp.l  #$48e7fffe,2(a0)
                beq    SID1_Init_ok
    nextinitloop:
                addq.l #1,a0            <-- steps ONE byte
                dbra   d1,initloop

Stepping one byte puts a0 on odd addresses, where both the cmp.w and the cmp.l
are misaligned. That is legal on a 68020 and an ADDRESS ERROR on a 68000. UADE
never trips over it because its uaerc sets cpu_type=68020; on a real A500 the
format dies in InitPlayer. SidMon 1.0 is an A500 tracker, so this is a limitation
of UADE's WRAPPER, not of the format.

WHY THE PATCH IS EQUIVALENT. The signature being searched for is 68k code, so it
can only ever begin at an even address. Stepping 2 finds the same first match and
never lands on an odd address. The loop count is unchanged, so the scan simply
covers twice the span; a genuine match is found at the same place.

WHY PATCHED AND NOT REBUILT. amigasrc/players/sidmon1/SIDMon1.0.s is INCOMPLETE:
checkloop1, songendfunc1 and songendfunc2 are referenced but never defined, and
it assembles to 830 bytes against the shipped 952. A rebuild cannot be verified
against upstream, so a source-level fix could not be trusted. A one-word patch to
the shipped binary can be stated exactly, which is what this file does.

Restore the original with:
    cp /opt/homebrew/share/uade/players/SIDMon1.0 .
